  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>

    <div class="page-shell">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Feline essentials</p>
        <h1>Cat FAQ</h1>
        <p class="intro">
          Quick answers for curious cat people, from purring and playtime to
          litter boxes and whiskers.
        </p>
      </header>

      <main id="main">
        <div class="faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
          <div class="example">
            <button
              class="question"
              type="button"
              aria-expanded="false"
              aria-controls="answer-purr"
            >
              <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="details" id="answer-purr" hidden>
              <p>
                Cats often purr when they feel relaxed or content, but purring
                can also happen when they are stressed, injured, or asking for
                attention. The sound is a flexible way cats communicate and
                self-soothe.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="example">
            <button
              class="question"
              type="button"
              aria-expanded="false"
              aria-controls="answer-knead"
            >
              <span>Why do cats knead with their paws?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="details" id="answer-knead" hidden>
              <p>
                Kneading starts in kittenhood when kittens press their mother's
                belly to encourage milk flow. Adult cats may keep the behavior
                because it is comforting, marks a favorite spot with scent, or
                helps them settle down.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="example">
            <button
              class="question"
              type="button"
              aria-expanded="false"
              aria-controls="answer-sleep"
            >
              <span>How much do cats sleep?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="details" id="answer-sleep" hidden>
              <p>
                Many cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day, and kittens or senior
                cats may sleep even more. Their natural hunting rhythm favors
                short bursts of activity followed by plenty of rest.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="example">
            <button
              class="question"
              type="button"
              aria-expanded="false"
              aria-controls="answer-litter"
            >
              <span>How often should I clean a litter box?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="details" id="answer-litter" hidden>
              <p>
                Scoop waste at least once a day and replace litter regularly
                according to the litter type. A clean box helps prevent odors
                and makes it more likely your cat will use it reliably.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="example">
            <button
              class="question"
              type="button"
              aria-expanded="false"
              aria-controls="answer-whiskers"
            >
              <span>What are cat whiskers for?</span>
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <div class="details" id="answer-whiskers" hidden>
              <p>
                Whiskers are sensitive touch sensors that help cats judge
                spaces, detect nearby movement, and navigate in low light.
                They should never be trimmed because they support balance and
                spatial awareness.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </main>

      <footer>
        <p>Tip: Use Tab to move through questions, then press Enter or Space to expand an answer.</p>
      </footer>
    </div>

    <script>
      const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

      questions.forEach((question) => {
        question.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const detailsId = question.getAttribute("aria-controls");
          const details = document.getElementById(detailsId);
          const isExpanded = question.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

          question.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
          details.hidden = isExpanded;
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
